\section{Data Structures}

\subsection{Interrupt State}

Tracks whether IRQ and NMI are enabled.  The game toggles these via I/O
ports 0x4C/0x4D (NMI) and 0x4F (IRQ).

We also count how many IRQs and NMIs were actually fired per frame for
diagnostic purposes.

<<interrupt state struct>>=
struct InterruptState {
    bool nmi_enabled = false;
    bool irq_enabled = false;

    // Diagnostics (reset each frame)
    int irq_count = 0;
    int nmi_count = 0;
};
@

\subsection{Frame Event}

Each event in the per-frame table specifies a cycle offset and the type
of interrupt to fire.

<<frame event struct>>=
enum class IntType : uint8_t { NMI, IRQ };

struct FrameEvent {
    int cycle_offset;
    IntType type;
    uint8_t vcounter;   // for V256 tracking
    bool v256;          // whether this event is in vblank region
};
@

