\section{Frame Runner}

The [[run\_frame]] function executes one full frame of Z80 code.  It runs
the CPU in chunks between interrupt events, firing the appropriate
interrupt at each boundary.  The function updates the video [[v256]] flag
at each event to track the beam position for port 0x4E reads.

The function is declared to take the CPU, interrupt state, and video state.
The Z80 class is forward-declared here to avoid a circular include
dependency; the implementation file includes both headers.

<<run frame declaration>>=
class Z80;
struct VideoState;

int run_frame(Z80& cpu, InterruptState& ints, VideoState& video);
@

